WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.630
Ever since The Walt Disney Company announced
its plans to acquire the majority of studio

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:12.139
20th Century Fox's assets in a $71.3 billion
merger set to be completed in 2019, one question

00:00:12.139 --> 00:00:16.810
that has been on every superhero fan's mind
is whether or not Marvel Studios would recast

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:17.980
members of the X-Men.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.720
After all, Disney's purchase of Fox does include
the entire slate of mutants who will soon

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.840
join the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.820
And just about no X-Man is more beloved than
Wolverine.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:31.220
"Cuz I'm the best there is at what I do.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.700
But what I do best isn't very nice."

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:37.370
Curiosity about such a recasting turned to
foaming-at-the-mouth excitement when longtime

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:42.969
X-Men film franchise producer Lauren Shuler
Donner told Slashfilm in February 2019 that

00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:47.530
Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige would
start scouting for a younger actor to play

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:51.230
the next Wolverine as soon as the Disney-Fox
merger goes through.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:55.680
From there, the internet kicked into overdrive
imagining who that younger actor might be.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.500
And as odd as it sounds at first, social media
frequenters are unironically loving the idea

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.120
of Harry Potter series star Daniel Radcliffe
stepping up to portray the new Wolverine,

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:10.520
assuming the role that Australian actor Hugh
Jackman played from 2000 until 2017.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:14.680
Piggy-backing off all the online chatter,
digital artist BossLogic created stunning

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:19.080
artwork imagining what Radcliffe could look
like as the hard-bitten, nearly indestructible

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:19.600
hero.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:23.240
Though there's really no predicting which
actor Feige and the Marvel team will end up

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.660
tapping — and no one involved at either
Marvel or Fox has commented on the plausibility

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:32.480
of Radcliffe taking the role — the entire
situation actually started as a joke.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.960
The idea gained popularity after Radcliffe
participated in a Wired Autocomplete Interview.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:41.720
After answering a few Harry Potter-themed
questions, Radcliffe tackled the subject of

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:43.900
whether he is, in fact, the new Wolverine.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:48.100
"There's gonna be a new Wolverine movie in
which it starts off with Hugh Jackman being

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.750
put into a hot wash.

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:51.540
And then when he comes out, it's me.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:52.580
So yes!"

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:56.440
Radcliffe's joking tone made his answer seem
like total farce, but comic book fans were

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:00.300
quick to ponder whether the Harry Potter alum
could actually be telling the truth.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:04.880
And surprisingly, a lot of people were down
for it, with a vast majority of Twitter users

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:09.009
arguing that Radcliffe would simply need to
bulk up before formally joining the X-Men

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:10.060
movie world.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.340
One fan wrote in response,

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.340
"That could work.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:17.230
Give him a year of protein shakes, growth
hormone, steak, creatine, testosterone injections,

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:21.560
chicken, rice, trained by The Mountain in
Iceland, and also eat lots of crumpets…

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:22.560
yeah that would work.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:23.360
It's doable.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:23.900
That would be awesome."

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.180
Another added that if British actor Tom Holland
can play the American superhero Spider-Man,

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:32.300
there's nothing stopping England-born Radcliffe
from portraying Wolverine.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:36.310
A few fans who live and die by comic book
accuracy even noted that Radcliffe might be

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:41.260
better suited than Jackman ever was in one
regard: Wolverine is five-foot-three, while

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.960
Radcliffe is 5'6" and Jackman is a staggering
6'2".

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.940
Sadly, though, what began as a joke remains
just that.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.860
Radcliffe has since come forward to clarify
his statements and make it crystal clear that

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:55.900
he isn't playing Wolverine — no confirmation
from Disney or Fox needed.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:01.800
Speaking to IGN for a recent interview discussing
his new project, the TBS show Miracle Workers,

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:02.340
Radcliffe shared,

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.100
"This is what happens when you make jokes.

00:03:10.569 --> 00:03:14.350
So, there you have it: Radcliffe won't become
the man behind the mutant.

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:18.180
But hey, if the internet didn't hate the thought
of pint-sized Radcliffe rising to serve as

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.400
the next Wolverine, it seems people may be
open to hearing other outside-the-box-ideas

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:27.460
— so long as the actor doesn't mind chugging
protein shakes and working out eleventeen hours a day.

